        <body>
            <div xml:id="d562">

                <pb facs="0503" n="387" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg387"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 738.3915/183.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Dominican Chargé
                        d’Affaires</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-12-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 13, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge with
                    thanks the receipt of the Minister’s note of the 22d ultimo, in which he
                    encloses for the information of the Department a record of the minutes
                    [etc.].</p>
                <p>The Department notes that since July 13 of this year there has been no exchange
                    of views between the Plenipotentiaries other than the exchange shown in the
                    remarks recorded under date of August 8 last, enclosed by Señor Peynado as
                    enclosures two and three in his note.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.],</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
